<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">Privacy</h1><p class="ref-lede">The Epoch Institute collects as little as it can. This page says what, why, for how long, and how to change your mind. Last updated 8 November 2026.</p></header>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Who is responsible</h2><p>The Epoch Institute (the-epoch-institute.org), an independent project run by its editor. For anything about your data, write to <a href="mailto:info@the-epoch-institute.org">info@the-epoch-institute.org</a>.</p></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec" id="cookies"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Counting readers: Google Analytics</h2><p>The Institute uses Google Analytics to count visits: which pages are read, from what kind of device, and from which country. It also counts a few actions without saying who took them: a game finished, a page shared, Listen started, a link to a source or to a suggested next page followed, an answer to &#8220;Was this page useful?&#8221;, a newsletter sign-up. It helps decide what to write next.</p><ul><li>Until you choose, and if you choose <b>No thanks</b>, Analytics sets no cookies: Google receives only anonymous signals without identifiers (Google&#8217;s consent mode).</li><li>If you choose <b>Allow</b>, Analytics sets its cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) to recognise a returning browser. Google Analytics does not store IP addresses.</li><li>Kids mode never sets these cookies, whatever was chosen.</li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Change your choice</h2><p><button type="button" class="hero-cta" data-consent-open>Change cookie settings</button></p><p>The choice is kept in your browser (<code>epoch-consent</code>). Clearing your browser&#8217;s site data resets it.</p></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">What stays in your browser</h2><p>Your settings (theme, Kids mode), the pages you have read, your shelf, your game scores and streaks, your flashcards, the pages you have marked useful or not, and your Passport are kept in your own browser&#8217;s storage (localStorage). They are never sent to the Institute. Clear them from My Passport (<a href="/passport">Clear</a>) or your browser&#8217;s settings.</p></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">What you send us</h2><p>The contact form, article submissions, applications and newsletter sign-ups go to the Institute&#8217;s own mail handler, which emails them to the Institute&#8217;s mailboxes.</p><ul><li>A copy of each message is kept on the server for 30 days, then deleted.</li><li>Newsletter addresses are kept in the subscriber list until you ask to leave (reply &#8220;unsubscribe&#8221; to any issue, or write to us).</li><li>An answer to &#8220;Was this page useful?&#8221; is counted by the same handler as the page and a yes or no, with the time; it is not emailed and nothing about you is kept with it. To limit spam, the handler keeps a scrambled (hashed) form of the sender&#8217;s IP address for a day; it cannot be turned back into the address.</li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Supporting the Institute</h2><p>Support payments are made on <a href="https://ko-fi.com/the_epoch_institute" rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a>, which handles the payment through Stripe or PayPal. The Institute never sees your card details. Ko-fi passes on your name, email and any message you write, so we can thank you. Ko-fi&#8217;s own privacy policy covers what it keeps.</p></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Other services the pages use</h2><ul><li><b>Cloudflare</b> delivers the site&#8217;s pages and files, and protects it from attacks; like any web server, it processes your IP address to do so.</li><li><b>The hosting company</b> keeps standard server logs.</li><li><b>YouTube</b> performances on the song pages load from youtube-nocookie.com, and only when you press play. <b>Genius</b> lyrics load only when you press their button.</li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Your rights</h2><p>You may ask what the Institute holds about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or object to its use: write to <a href="mailto:info@the-epoch-institute.org">info@the-epoch-institute.org</a>. If you are in the UK you may also complain to the Information Commissioner&#8217;s Office (ico.org.uk); in the EU, to your national data protection authority.</p><p>The legal bases are your consent (analytics cookies), the Institute&#8217;s legitimate interest in answering messages and keeping the site safe (forms, logs), and, for the newsletter, your request to receive it.</p></section>
<section class="ws-guide-sec"><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Children</h2><p>The site is free to read for all ages. Kids mode sets no analytics cookies and shows no prompts to pay. The forms are meant for adults: we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p></section>
